.TH ARPWATCHDOG 1 "2026-11-16" "arpwatchdog 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arpwatchdog \- passive ARP spoofing detector for local networks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arpwatchdog
[\fB\-i\fR \fIIFACE\fR | \fB\-r\fR \fIFILE\fR | \fB\-p\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arpwatchdog
watches IP\-to\-MAC mapping changes, rapid MAC flip\-flops and gateway MAC
moves — the classic signatures of ARP poisoning / MITM attacks — and emits
structured alerts in real time.
.PP
It is strictly passive: it never sends ARP probes, never scans and never
injects packets. Capture requires raw\-socket privileges; prefer
.B setcap cap_net_raw
on a dedicated interpreter over running as root.
.PP
A mapping change is a signal to investigate, not proof of attack. DHCP
renewals, router failover, virtualization and hardware replacement produce
legitimate changes.
.SH MODES
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interface " " \fIIFACE\fR
Capture ARP/ND/DHCP live on \fIIFACE\fR (requires scapy). The default gateway
is auto\-detected from the routing table unless \fB\-\-gateway\fR is given.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-replay " " \fIFILE\fR
Replay JSONL records
.RS
 {"interface":"eth0","timestamp":1730000000.5,"frame_hex":"..."}
.RE
from \fIFILE\fR; \fB\-\fR or omission reads stdin.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pcap " " \fIFILE\fR
Replay observations from a saved pcap/pcapng capture (requires scapy).
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the learned IP/MAC table after processing.
.TP
.B \-\-export " " \fIFORMAT FILE\fR
Export the learned inventory as \fBjson\fR, \fBcsv\fR, \fBhtml\fR or \fBmd\fR.
.SH DETECTIONS
.TP
.B new_host
First claim for an address (severity: info).
.TP
.B mapping_changed
An IP now claims a different MAC (warning); carries
\fBip_conflict\fR when two MACs claim the address inside the flip window and
\fBflip_flop\fP with rapid alternation evidence (critical).
.TP
.B gateway_mac_changed
A watched gateway MAC moved (critical).
.SH ALERTING
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIjson|text|csv\fR
Alert rendering (default json).
.TP
.BR \-\-alert\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Append alerts to \fIFILE\fR; \fB\-\-alert\-max\-bytes\fR rotates it.
.TP
.B \-\-syslog
Send alerts to the system logger (LOG_CRIT for critical events).
.TP
.BR \-\-webhook " " \fIURL\fR
POST each alert as JSON; failures are counted, never fatal.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
No stdout alerts (combine with sinks above).
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics\-file " " \fIPATH\fR ", " \-\-metrics\-serve " " \fI[HOST:]PORT\fR
Prometheus metrics snapshot or HTTP endpoint (opt\-in; bind localhost).
.TP
.BR \-\-fail\-on " " \fIcritical\fR
Exit code 3 when any critical alert fired (CI pipelines).
.SH TUNING
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore " " \fICIDR\fR
Never alert for this range (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-suppress\-window " " \fISEC\fR
Dedup window per (event, ip); flip\-flop evidence bypasses it.
.TP
.BR \-\-flip\-window " " \fISEC\fR ", " \-\-flip\-changes " " \fIN\fR
Flip\-flop thresholds (default 300s / 3 changes).
.TP
.BR \-\-baseline " " \fIFILE\fR
arpwatch arp.dat baseline (mac ip per line).
.TP
.BR \-\-state " " \fIFILE\fR
Persist learned mappings across restarts (atomic JSON).
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE.toml\fR
Default options from TOML; CLI flags override.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Count events, emit nothing. \fB\-\-debug\fR logs pipeline decisions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No critical alerts (or \-\-fail\-on none).
.TP
.B 2
Usage/configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Critical alert(s) emitted and \-\-fail\-on critical.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I examples/arpwatchdog.toml
Annotated configuration example.
.TP
.I deploy/arpwatchdog.service
Hardened systemd unit (CAP_NET_RAW only, DynamicUser).
.SH SEE ALSO
arpwatch(8), addrwatch(1)
.PP
Repository: https://github.com/navairgap/arpwatchdog
